{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"defaultSize","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"_","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"size","kind":"internalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/Size","text":"Size","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:11OpenSwiftUI4SizeV"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"some","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/Scene","text":"Scene","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:11OpenSwiftUI5SceneP"},{"text":"\n","kind":"text"}],"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"parameters","parameters":[{"name":"size","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The default size for new windows created from a scene.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"content":[{"anchor":"return-value","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Return Value"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A scene that uses a default size for new windows.","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"},{"content":[{"anchor":"discussion","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Discussion"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Use this scene modifier to indicate a default initial size for a new"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"window that the system creates from a "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/Scene"},{"type":"text","text":" declaration. For"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"example, you can request that new windows that a "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/WindowGroup"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"generates occupy 600 points in the x-dimension and 400 points in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the y-dimension:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":null,"code":["@main","struct MyApp: App {","    var body: some Scene {","        WindowGroup {","            ContentView()","        }","        .defaultSize(CGSize(width: 600, height: 400))","    }","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The size that you specify acts only as a default for when the window"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"first appears. People can later resize the window using interface"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"controls that the system provides. Also, during state restoration,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the system restores windows to their most recent size rather than"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the default size."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"If you specify a default size that’s outside the range of the window’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"inherent resizability in one or both dimensions, the system clamps the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"affected dimension to keep it in range. You can configure the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"resizability of a scene using the ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/Scene\/windowResizability(_:)","type":"reference"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"modifier.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The default size modifier affects any scene type that creates windows","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"in macOS, namely:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/WindowGroup","isActive":true,"type":"reference"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"Window","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"DocumentGroup","type":"codeVoice"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Settings"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If you want to specify the input directly in terms of width and height,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"use "},{"code":"Scene\/defaultSize(width:height:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" instead."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"metadata":{"symbolKind":"method","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"defaultSize","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"Size","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:11OpenSwiftUI4SizeV"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"some","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Scene","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:11OpenSwiftUI5SceneP"}],"modules":[{"name":"OpenSwiftUI"}],"role":"symbol","title":"defaultSize(_:)","roleHeading":"Instance Method","extendedModule":"OpenSwiftUI","externalID":"s:11OpenSwiftUI5ScenePAAE11defaultSizeyQrAA0F0VF::SYNTHESIZED::s:11OpenSwiftUI11WindowGroupV"},"kind":"symbol","sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/openswiftui\/windowgroup\/defaultsize(_:)"]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/WindowGroup\/defaultSize(_:)","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI","doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/WindowGroup"]]},"abstract":[{"text":"Sets a default size for a window.","type":"text"}],"references":{"doc://OpenSwiftUI/documentation/OpenSwiftUI/WindowGroup":{"url":"\/documentation\/openswiftui\/windowgroup","kind":"symbol","type":"topic","title":"WindowGroup","identifier":"doc:\/\/OpenSwiftUI\/documentation\/OpenSwiftUI\/WindowGrou